# Publish idk on every commit or update

Whenever you commit, push, update a release, or ship idk, raise the version first, then build that same source into the installer. Do this before you tell the user the update is ready. Do not wait to be asked. Do not ship two commits on the same version.

The version is one number. If the user did not name the next one, raise the patch number. Write that same number in every place below before you package. Do not leave the previous number in any of them.

- `installer/idk.iss`: `MyAppVersion` and `VersionInfoVersion`. A version `0.1.1` has `VersionInfoVersion` `0.1.1.0`.
- `Idk/Idk.csproj`: `Version`, `AssemblyVersion`, `FileVersion`, and `InformationalVersion`. `AssemblyVersion` and `FileVersion` use four parts, such as `0.1.1.0`.
- `website/download.html`: the version text.
- `README.md`: `dist-setup/idk-Setup-<version>.exe`.
- `brain/log.json`: this commit's notes go on a new top entry for that version, dated today. Leave shipped versions as they are. If the top entry is still the shipped version, add the new entry and move the unreleased notes into it.

1. Raise the version in the list above. Add any unlogged change to that new `brain/log.json` entry under `added` or `fixes`.
2. Update `README.md` so the version and the installer path `dist-setup/idk-Setup-<version>.exe` match this build.
3. Rebuild with `powershell -File scripts/package-windows.ps1`. The setup file is `dist-setup/idk-Setup-<version>.exe`. The script also copies it to `website/download/idk-Setup.exe`.
4. Never commit `.env` or `billing.env`. The installer must not contain them.
5. Do not print tokens or license secrets from `.env`.
6. When the user says commit, commit and update, or update the latest changes, that request includes GitHub. Push `main` to `https://github.com/Delexoo/idk` in the same turn as the commit. Do not stop after a local commit. Use `GITHUB_TOKEN` from `D:\MasterVault\idk\.env` and do not print the token. If git reports dubious ownership, pass `-c safe.directory=D:/MasterVault/idk`. Do not change git config.
7. Run `node scripts/render-release-notes.mjs` so `website/releases.html` lists every version in `brain/log.json`. Each version keeps its own added and fixes lines. Do not skip a version and do not merge several versions into one note.
8. Run `node scripts/post-release-notes.mjs` with `GITHUB_TOKEN` from `.env`. It creates or updates a GitHub release for every version in the log, and the body is that version's notes. Do not print the token.
9. Deploy the `website` folder to the Vercel project `idk` on team `trymoonrises-projects` with `node scripts/deploy-site.mjs`. It uses `VERCEL_TOKEN` from `.env`. Do not print the token. `website/.vercel` stays uncommitted. The live site is `https://idk-trymoonrises-projects.vercel.app`.
10. Stop when `https://idk-trymoonrises-projects.vercel.app/releases.html` includes the current version.
